<Base title="Brand & technology" description="Learn about AUTO Tailor automotive film materials and construction.">
  <section class="page-heading wrap narrow-heading"><span class="section-label">Brand &amp; technology</span><h1>A tailored approach to automotive film.</h1><p>AUTO Tailor takes its name from tailoring: selecting materials and applying them to suit the vehicle.</p></section>
  <section class="wide-image wrap"><img src="/images/color-wrap.webp" alt="Color film being applied to a vehicle" /></section>
  <section class="section wrap detail-section"><div><span class="section-label">Paint protection</span><h2>Built in layers.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>The paint protection catalog illustrates a layered construction that includes a repair coating, TPU base and pressure-sensitive adhesive. The construction and thickness vary by product.</p><p>The catalog describes heat-assisted scratch repair for the listed films. Repair performance depends on the type and depth of the damage and the conditions of use.</p></div></section>
  <section class="material-band"><div class="wrap material-grid"><div><span class="section-label">Color TPU</span><h2>Color meets protection.</h2></div><div><p>The color TPU catalog describes a cast-grade composite structure with a TPU base, a color layer and a repair coating. Gloss and matte films are presented with different installation approaches.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap detail-section"><div><span class="section-label">Window film</span><h2>Different technologies, different choices.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>The window film catalog presents nano-ceramic, sputtered metal and metal-ceramic options. Each series lists shades with different visible light transmission and solar properties.</p><p>Film selection should take account of the vehicle, local tint regulations and the specifications for the actual product supplied.</p><a class="text-link" href="/products/#window-film">View window films <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
</Base>
